    "result_text": "The full suite is green (only `AcceptanceTest` contains executable tests; the other files under `acceptance/` are the base class and a log helper). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` field so the owner API returns `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing pattern used for the other computed owner fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto` backed by a new `toContactPreference` method that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner has a non-blank email and `\"PHONE\"` otherwise.\n\nBecause the field is populated in the mapper (used by both `getOwner` and the create path), it's returned consistently on `GET /api/owners/{id}`. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2).",
